course: dictionary
lesson: 4224
title: Names with capitals and words from far away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with a capital letter because they are names. Graham is a boy's or man's first name, and it can also be a family name. «Alexander Graham Bell patented the telephone in 1876.» Here Graham is part of a person's full name, so it has a capital letter.
explain: Some words look like ordinary words but are not. Graham also has a meaning as a food. «graham flour» and «graham cracker» are American words. In the US, a graham cracker is a sweet, flat biscuit made with wholemeal flour.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. Look for a capital letter, which often means a name. Look for words like flour, cracker or biscuit, which tell you it is about food. Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Graham is a first name and a family name for people.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a word often shows a name, such as Graham or Alexander.
fact: Graham flour is wholemeal wheat flour.
fact: A graham cracker is a sweet, flat wholemeal biscuit, mostly used in the United States.
fact: «Patented» means the inventor was given the official right to their invention.
exercise: In «Alexander Graham Bell patented the telephone in 1876», what kind of word is Graham? | A kind of flour | A place to visit | A biscuit | *A name
exercise: A recipe asks for graham flour. What is graham flour? | A kind of cake tin | Flour made from rice | White sugar | *Wholemeal wheat flour
exercise: Which is a graham cracker? | A kind of camping tent | *A sweet, flat wholemeal biscuit | A loud, old-fashioned bell | A bus that runs at night
test: Why does Graham start with a capital letter in «Alexander Graham Bell»? | Because it is a food | *Because it is a name | Because it starts a sentence | Because it is very important
test: The word «graham cracker» is used mostly in which country? | Scotland | South Africa | *United States | Australia
exam: In «Alexander Graham Bell patented the telephone in 1876», what does patented mean? | He lost it in a park | He broke it in 1876 | He ate a biscuit with it | *He was given the official right to it as his invention
